id=3D"reading"><article><h1 id=3D"passage-0">From Short Videos to Customers=
</h1>
<h2 id=3D"passage-1">A practical course in video craft, affiliate marketing=
, and digital-product funnels</h2>
<p id=3D"passage-2">Written for Aadil's strengths in software development, =
teaching, and technical writing. Start with an original demonstration that =
helps a viewer understand something useful. Then build an appropriate next =
step: an affiliate product, a free lesson, an ebook, or a working software =
experience.</p>
<p id=3D"passage-3">This book assumes no filming, editing, or marketing exp=
erience. Basic development knowledge helps with the examples but is not req=
uired to understand the marketing principles. The examples use browser exte=
nsions and coding education because they offer a credible way to connect yo=
ur ability to build with your ability to explain. Product names, prices, sc=
ripts, and business datasets are hypothetical unless identified as a docume=
nted source case.</p>
<p id=3D"passage-4">The first half teaches ideas, scripting, filming, sound=
, screen demonstrations, editing, deliberate practice, learning resources, =
and AI assistance. The second half teaches affiliate economics, TikTok Shop=
, owned Shopify routes, email, YouTube Shorts handoffs, SaaS activation, me=
asurement, and operations. Complete chapters are included; the course is no=
t just an outline.</p>
<p id=3D"passage-5">Read in order the first time. Use the resource map to s=
elect one editing path and make projects while studying. The optional 180-h=
our plan includes production and experimentation time, not 180 hours of lec=
ture text. Its practice blocks overlap the suggested chapter apprenticeship=
s; they are not additional mandatory schedules. The ninety-day plan is an a=
lternative implementation rhythm.</p>
<p id=3D"passage-6"><strong>Research baseline:</strong> November 13, 2026, =
primarily United States rules. Account access, regions, categories, agreeme=
nts, and software tiers differ. The source appendix explicitly distinguishe=
s inspected policy text, partially inspected pages, course indexes, and una=
vailable material. No training course is claimed completed merely because i=
ts index was read. A separate Deep Research job was not available; research=
 used multi-query web retrieval and official sources.</p>
<p id=3D"passage-7"><strong>Your starting experiment:</strong> make a small=
 series for developers learning useful browser projects; offer one strong s=
ample lesson; validate a finished narrow ebook; recommend only tools you ca=
n evaluate honestly. A SaaS route is taught as another option, with activat=
ion and retention as central requirements. This is a suggested sequence to =
test, not an earnings promise.</p>
<p id=3D"passage-8">Use the offline workbook to estimate script timing, ins=
pect a vertical caption layout, explore funnel economics, construct campaig=
n links, model SaaS retention, and examine conversion uncertainty. The work=
book performs the displayed arithmetic locally. It does not inspect actual =
footage, operate a checkout, publish videos, or predict virality.</p>
<p id=3D"passage-9">The standalone HTML edition contains both the complete =
textbook and the workbook. The portable package also contains the numbered =
Markdown chapters, sources, templates, readable companion source, and verif=
ication evidence. Named vendor tools and live commerce services were resear=
ched but not executed; the local companion is tested separately.</p>
